00:26:00.170 --> 00:26:03.210
So the purpose of the traffic impact study is to determine

00:26:03.690 --> 00:26:06.410
if the land develop proposal event land development

00:26:06.730 --> 00:26:09.850
has any impact on the adjacent road roadway network.

00:26:10.170 --> 00:26:16.505
And if it does, we recommend any type of mitigation that is needed. So for the analysis, we usually perform three

00:26:16.745 --> 00:26:17.625
scenarios,

00:26:17.625 --> 00:26:19.945
existing conditions as they are today,

00:26:20.345 --> 00:26:21.705
no build conditions,

00:26:21.705 --> 00:26:26.905
which means in the future year without the build without the proposed development,

00:26:27.180 --> 00:26:29.740
and build conditions with the proposed development.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:32.860
For this particular development, we considered

00:26:32.860 --> 00:26:34.380
three time frames,

00:26:34.940 --> 00:26:38.700
where we looked at the morning peak hour, which is between seven and 8AM,

00:26:39.420 --> 00:26:45.855
afternoon peak hour, weekday afternoon peak hour between four to five p. M. And on Saturday midday,

00:26:46.015 --> 00:26:47.135
which is your peaking

00:26:47.855 --> 00:26:49.055
shopping period.

00:26:49.935 --> 00:26:52.255
So again, this is just a site from

00:26:52.735 --> 00:26:53.855
a different viewpoint.

00:26:55.050 --> 00:26:55.690
So

00:26:56.010 --> 00:26:59.930
when we do the analysis, we look at intersection geometry,

00:26:59.930 --> 00:27:04.170
traffic control devices such as signal controls and volumes

00:27:04.490 --> 00:27:05.690
on the roadway.

00:27:05.690 --> 00:27:08.970
We collected traffic count information in 2022

00:27:09.665 --> 00:27:16.225
within the last few weeks, and we also applied an annual growth rate of 1% for future years.

00:27:19.345 --> 00:27:26.990
Noble conditions, as I mentioned before, represent the conditions without the project itself. However, they do take into account that one year

00:27:27.310 --> 00:27:28.430
of growth,

00:27:28.430 --> 00:27:29.550
which is one percent.

00:27:30.750 --> 00:27:33.630
We have also discussed that with the we reached out to the

00:27:34.045 --> 00:27:40.045
Connecticut DOT as well as the town to find out if there are any other projects in the area that we should consider in the traffic

00:27:40.525 --> 00:27:42.285
report, and there were none.

00:27:43.245 --> 00:27:44.365
So that said,

00:27:44.925 --> 00:27:45.885
we utilize

00:27:46.205 --> 00:27:48.205
ITE trip generation manual

00:27:48.620 --> 00:27:50.300
that provides us with

00:27:51.340 --> 00:27:52.860
potential proposed

00:27:52.860 --> 00:27:55.660
trips generated by the proposed development.

00:27:56.140 --> 00:28:00.860
In this instance, we're looking again at AM peak period, PM, and Saturday.

00:28:01.020 --> 00:28:05.475
So the development, the proposed development with the square footage of 10,000

00:28:05.635 --> 00:28:06.595
square feet

00:28:06.915 --> 00:28:08.835
generates about 25,000

00:28:08.835 --> 00:28:11.715
trips in the morning. That's 14 entering

00:28:11.875 --> 00:28:12.915
and 11

00:28:13.475 --> 00:28:14.275
exiting.

00:28:14.435 --> 00:28:15.555
56

00:28:15.555 --> 00:28:16.835
trips during peak period

00:28:18.220 --> 00:28:20.620
with 29 entering and 27

00:28:21.340 --> 00:28:22.060
exiting.

00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:23.580
And on Saturday,

00:28:24.300 --> 00:28:27.420
since the manual does not provide an actual

00:28:29.020 --> 00:28:30.540
peak hour time, we

00:28:31.180 --> 00:28:33.420
estimate that it's one and a half times of peak,

00:28:34.055 --> 00:28:34.935
which means

00:28:35.255 --> 00:28:38.455
we've estimated the trips to be 84

00:28:39.415 --> 00:28:40.935
during that timeframe.

00:28:41.495 --> 00:28:43.895
So now having those trips generated by

00:28:44.135 --> 00:28:47.095
the proposed development, distribute it across the network.

00:28:49.990 --> 00:28:55.270
So when we distribute them across the network, we utilize a software called Syncro

00:28:55.590 --> 00:28:59.270
that provides us with level of service, how well the

